# Comments, escaping, and whitespace

```rocci
## Greeting used by the page.
@component Hello = |{ name }|
    <p>Hello, {name}</p>
```

| Form | Where | Effect |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `#` at start of a template item | Template body | Line comment |
| `<!-- … -->` | Template body | Dropped HTML comment |
| `@@` | Template body | Literal `@` |
| `## ` immediately above top-level `@` | File | Doc comment attached to generated assignment |
| Roc `#` | Roc regions | Ordinary Roc comment |

`## ` must sit immediately above the declaration (no blank line). Those lines
are also the attached docs `rocci-docs` copies onto generated example source
pages.

Indentation-only whitespace around tags is discarded. Inline spaces in
`Hello, {name}` are kept.

**Related:** [Examples declaration docs](/examples/).
